    "text": "2448 rows. That's a lot. I need to judge every row. That's a huge task. Let me structure it: parse the CSV, and process in chunks. Each row requires careful reasoning by me (the model). 2448 rows is very large — I need to be efficient but fair.\n\nStrategy: dump the rows in manageable chunks (e.g., 60-80 rows at a time) with n, text, sop, alt, and reason. Total CSV 151KB, so text+sop+alt avg ~60 bytes per row... wait 151380/2449 ≈ 62 bytes per row. Hmm that seems small. Actually many rows are probably short. Let me check the size distribution.\n\nActually wait — 151KB / 2448 = 62 bytes per row, but the first row was already ~2000 bytes. So many rows must be very short (probably empty sop and alt). Let me check.\n\nLet me load the CSV and print stats.",
