 with 'calendar' as its complement and 'please' as a discourse word.\",None),\n(27,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'make a calendar for Podcast' is a command, with 'something warm-coloured' tied to the calendar by a relation without a marker.\",None),\n(28,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'any colour that isn't used yet' is a relative clause tied to 'colour', with 'is' as auxiliary, 'n't' as negation and 'used' as verb.\",None),\n(29,\"L8\",\"Accepted: the verbless part 'one more calendar, mint colour' is a fragment whose two nominals are tied by a relation.\",None),\n(33,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'call the Family calendar Home' is a command with 'from now on' held as a relation marked 'from' starting at the clause.\",None),\n(38,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'if nobody minds' is tied to the commands 'rename Family to Household' and 'make it green', with 'green' a modifier of its clause.\",None),\n(39,\"L1\",\"'the kids keep asking' states something and is no question, yet it is written form=interrogative, and the reported question 'which calendar is theirs' is written interrogative where it states and should be declarative.\",'''@n1 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"kids\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=declarative verb=\"keep\" subject=$n1\n@c2 syntax.clause form=nonfinite verb=\"asking\"\n@r1 syntax.relation from=$c1 to=$c2\n@n2 syntax.nominal dependent=\"which\" head=\"calendar\"\n@c3 syntax.clause form=declarative verb=\"is\" subject=$n2 complement=$n3\n@n3 syntax.nominal head=\"theirs\"\n@r2 syntax.relation from=$c2 to=$c3\n@n4 syntax.nominal head=\"you\"\n@n5 syntax.nominal dependent=\"Kids\" head=\"stuff\"\n@c4 syntax.clause form=interrogative auxiliary=\"could\" verb=\"rename\" subject=$n4 complement=$n5\n@r3 syntax.relation marker=\"to\" from=$c4 to=$k1\n@n6 syntax.nominal head=\"School\"\n@n7 syntax.nominal head=\"clubs\"\n@k1 syntax.coordination conjunction=\"and\" conjunct=$n6 conjunct=$n7'''),\n(40,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'the name Work is confusing now that I freelance too' is a clause with 'Work' tied to 'name', and the command 'change it to Agency work' carries 'hmm' and 'thanks' as discourse words.\",None),\n(47,\"L3\",\"'rename that one Hobbies' names two things, the thing renamed and the new name, but 'Hobbies' is written as the head of the nominal that holds 'that one', so the object of 'rename' is lost as a nominal.\",'''@c1 syntax.clause form=imperative verb=\"rename\" complement=$n1 complement=$n2\n@n1 syntax.nominal dependent=\"that\" head=\"one\"\n@n2 syntax.nominal head=\"Hobbies\"'''),\n(51,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'I'd like Work shown in purple' has 'I' as subject with the auxiliary of the contraction, 'Work' held as a fragment tied to the nonfinite 'shown', and 'in purple' tied to it.\",None),\n(57,\"L3\",\"In 'ok so paint the Gym calendar black and move yoga onto it' the word 'so' joins nothing that stands before it, yet it is held as one of the conjunctions of the coordination between the two commands.\",'''@c1 syntax.clause form=imperative discourse=\"ok\" discourse=\"so\" verb=\"paint\" modifier=\"black\" complement=$n1\n@k1 syntax.coordination conjunction=\"and\" conjunct=$c1 conjunct=$c2\n@n1 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" dependent=\"Gym\" head=\"calendar\"\n@c2 syntax.clause form=imperative verb=\"move\" complement=$n2\n@n2 syntax.nominal head=\"yoga\"\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"onto\" from=$c2 to=$n3\n@n3 syntax.nominal head=\"it\"'''),\n]\nwith open('meetings-07-advanced.p01.verdicts.jsonl','w') as f:\n    for n,g,note,sop in rows:\n        d={\"n\":n,\"grade\":g,\"note\":note}\n        if sop: d[\"sop\"]=sop\n        f.write(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False)+\"\\n\")\nprint(sum(1 for _ in open('meetings-07-advanced.p01.verdicts.jsonl')))\nPYEOF",
