dar room to building A' and 'rename it Cedar A' are commands joined by 'and' with their complements and relations intact.\",None),\n(224,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'ca' and 'n't' hold the negation of 'find', and 'would you note that it's behind reception, past the coffee machine?' carries the reported clause with both relations from it.\",None),\n(225,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'if the Oak room really is in the basement now' is tied to the command 'please update', and 'where it is' states with 'where' as a modifier and is tied to that command.\",None),\n(226,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'after the office move' and 'at 40 King Street' are relations from the clause, '2nd floor' is tied to the address, and the question 'can you fix that?' keeps its parts.\",None),\n(227,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'this room moved upstairs' is written as one clause with 'this room' as subject, 'moved' as verb and 'upstairs' as a modifier, which the next layer can read on.\",None),\n(233,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'Board room moved to floor 9' keeps its clause, its subject and the relation marked 'to' with '9' tied to 'floor'.\",None),\n(236,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'please get rid of the board room' is a command with 'of the board room' tied to it.\",None),\n(238,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'the Focus pod' is the subject of the nonfinite 'removed' with 'as a room' tied to it.\",None),\n(243,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'if no one has the Library booked' is tied to 'you can delete that room', with 'booked' a nonfinite clause over 'the Library'.\",None),\n(244,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'the building closed the old Annex for good' and the question 'would you mind removing it from the rooms?' are joined, and 'from the rooms' starts at 'removing'.\",None),\n(245,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'nobody ever books the Focus pod' is one clause, and 'let' with 's' as its complement carries the nonfinite 'just delete it'.\",None),\n(247,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'no more Cedar room' is a verbless fragment with 'no more' as dependents of 'room'.\",None),\n(250,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'Board room - gone' is written as a nonfinite clause with 'Board room' as its subject, which the next layer can read as a fragment.\",None),\n(256,\"L8\",\"Accepted: the coordination 'Lee, Priya and Ana' is the end of 'with', and 'next Tuesday' and 'at 11' are tied to their clause.\",None),\n(257,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'with Mihai and Priya' is tied to the session, and 'on Dec 3' and 'at 3pm' place '3' with 'Dec'.\",None),\n(260,\"L1\",\"In 'a meeting called Hiring debrief' the name 'Hiring debrief' is split, and 'Hiring' is made the verb of a nonfinite clause, which is no verb here.\",'''@c1 syntax.clause form=imperative verb=\"create\" complement=$n1\n@n1 syntax.nominal dependent=\"a\" head=\"meeting\"\n@c2 syntax.clause form=nonfinite verb=\"called\" complement=$n2\n@n2 syntax.nominal dependent=\"Hiring\" head=\"debrief\"\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"with\" from=$n1 to=$k1\n@n3 syntax.nominal head=\"Priya\"\n@n4 syntax.nominal head=\"Ana\"\n@k1 syntax.coordination conjunction=\"and\" conjunct=$n3 conjunct=$n4\n@r2 syntax.relation attachment=ambiguous marker=\"on\" from=$c1 to=$n5\n@n5 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"24th\"\n@r3 syntax.relation attachment=ambiguous marker=\"at\" from=$c1 to=$n6\n@n6 syntax.nominal head=\"1pm\"\n@r4 syntax.relation from=$n1 to=$c2'''),\n(262,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'Ana's back from leave Monday' is a clause with 'Monday' as complement and 'from leave' tied to it, and 'Book a catch-up with her at 10' a command with its ties.\",None),\n(263,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'if Mihai and Lee are both around tomorrow morning' is a clause tied to the command 'put a quick sync with them in the calendar'.\",None),\n(265,\"L8\",\"Accepted: the coordination of the three names is the complement of 'get', and 'to talk about the offsite' and the question 'could you find a time on Wednesday?' are tied.\",None),\n(266,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'booking an hour with Lee next Monday at 3' carries its complements, and 'He asked to review the contract' is a clause with the infinitive tied to it.\",None),\n(268,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'a call with Mihai sometime this week' is a fragment with both phrases tied to 'call'.\",None),\n(276,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'the client can only do mornings' is joined by 'so' to 'let' with 's' as its complement and the nonfinite 'put the Kickoff meeting on Wednesday at 8:30'.\",None),\n(277,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'the retro should happen right after the sprint ends' is tied to 'think', and the question 'could you schedule a Retro on the 28th at 4pm with Lee?' keeps its three relations.\",None),\n(278,\"L1\",\"'meeting tomorrow at 2' has no verb, yet 'meeting' is written as the verb of a nonfinite clause, so a noun is made the verb and the fragment is lost.\",'''@n1 syntax.nominal head=\"meeting\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=fragment modifier=\"tomorrow\" complement=$n1\n@r1 syntax.relation attachment=ambiguous marker=\"at\" from=$c1 to=$n2\n@n2 syntax.nominal head=\"2\"'''),\n(279,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'Ops review Monday morning' is a fragment with 'Monday morning' tied to 'Ops review'.\",None),\n(282,\"L8\",\"Accepted: the question carries 'with Priya' and 'before lunch tomorrow', and 'Nothing longer' and 'she's busy' are placed as a fragment and a clause.\",None),\n(284,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'hour-long meeting with Ana on Thursday' is a fragment with both phrases tied to 'meeting'.\",None),\n(285,\"L1\",\"'block 3 hours for a Planning offsite' is a command whose first word 'block' can be a verb, but 'block' is held as a noun in a fragment, so the command is lost.\",'''@c1 syntax.clause form=imperative verb=\"block\" complement=$n1\n@n1 syntax.nominal dependent=\"3\" head=\"hours\"\n@r1 syntax.relation attachment=ambiguous marker=\"for\" from=$c1 to=$n2\n@n2 syntax.nominal dependent=\"a\" dependent=\"Planning\" head=\"offsite\"'''),\n(289,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'somewhere quiet' is held in the clause of 'need', 'for my interview with Priya on Wednesday at 11' is tied to it, and 'the Focus pod would be perfect' is a clause of its own.\",None),\n(291,\"L1\",\"'meeting with Mihai, Cedar room' has no verb, yet 'meeting' is written as the verb of a nonfinite clause, so a noun is made the verb and the fragment is lost.\",'''@n1 syntax.nominal head=\"Mihai\"\n@n2 syntax.nominal dependent=\"Cedar\" head=\"room\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=fragment complement=$n2\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"with\" from=$c1 to=$n1'''),\n(296,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'Ana and I are planning the holiday party' keeps its coordination as subject, and the question 'can you create a Party planning meeting with her on the Work calendar for next Monday at 4?' keeps its ties.\",None),\n(297,\"L1\",\"'meeting on the Work calendar tomorrow' has no verb, yet 'meeting' is written as the verb of a nonfinite clause, so a noun is made the verb and the fragment is lost.\",'''@n1 syntax.nominal head=\"meeting\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=fragment modifier=\"tomorrow\" complement=$n1\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"on\" from=$c1 to=$n2\n@n2 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" dependent=\"Work\" head=\"calendar\"'''),\n(298,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'family meeting Sunday' is a fragment with 'Sunday' tied to the meeting, and 'family calendar' held as a second complement.\",None),\n(299,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'add a Gym meeting with coach Dan' keeps its command and the relation marked 'with'.\",None),\n(300,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'bring the Q3 figures' is joined to the clause that holds 'the note', so the content of the note is written and tied in the sentence.\",None),\n(301,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'notes' is held as a fragment and 'discuss the vendor contract' joined beside the clause it belongs to, so every word is placed and the parts are tied.\",None),\n(302,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'add the note' takes the note as complement and 'Review the three shortlisted CVs' is a nonfinite clause tied to it.\",None),\n(303,\"L8\",\"Accepted: the second verb 'write' follows the auxiliary of the question and keeps 'in the notes' and the content clause 'that we'll go through the Q4 roadmap' tied to it.\",None),\n(304,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'with the agenda' holds the coordination 'Budget overrun and next steps' as its end.\",None),\n(305,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'note' may be read as a command word, and 'ask about delivery dates' is placed beside it with 'about delivery dates' tied to it.\",None),\n(306,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'in the notes' is tied to the nonfinite 'put', and 'Bring laptops for the demo' is tied to that clause with 'for the demo' in the clause.\",None),\n(307,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'attach the note' takes the note as complement and 'Dial-in code 4471' is tied to it with '4471' tied to 'code'.\",None),\n(308,\"L3\",\"The clause 'when you book our Monday 11am meeting' belongs with 'add a note', but the relation marked 'so when' starts it at 'Priya always forgets the slides', and 'Monday 11am' is left in a fragment of its own.\",'''@n1 syntax.nominal head=\"Priya\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=declarative modifier=\"always\" verb=\"forgets\" subject=$n1 complement=$n2\n@n2 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"slides\"\n@n3 syntax.nominal head=\"you\"\n@n4 syntax.nominal dependent=\"our\" dependent=\"Monday\" dependent=\"11am\" head=\"meeting\"\n@c2 syntax.clause form=declarative verb=\"book\" subject=$n3 complement=$n4\n@c3 syntax.clause form=imperative verb=\"add\" complement=$n5\n@n5 syntax.nominal dependent=\"a\" head=\"note\"\n@c4 syntax.clause form=nonfinite verb=\"saying\"\n@r1 syntax.relation from=$n5 to=$c4\n@n6 syntax.nominal head=\"Priya\"\n@c5 syntax.clause form=declarative verb=\"brings\" subject=$n6 complement=$n7\n@n7 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"slides\"\n@r2 syntax.relation from=$c4 to=$c5\n@r3 syntax.relation marker=\"when\" from=$c3 to=$c2\n@r4 syntax.relation marker=\"so\" from=$c1 to=$c3'''),\n(309,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'in the notes' is tied to 'jot down', and 'confirm the hotel booking' is placed beside it with 'the hotel booking' as its complement.\",None),\n(310,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'to talk pricing' is tied to the clause of 'meeting', and 'with the note that he wants the competitor analysis first' ties the reported clause to 'note'.\",None),\n(311,\"L3\",\"In 'book a Design sync with Ana tomorrow at 3 with notes Share Figma link, and cancel the yoga' the coordination and 'notes' hold both 'Share Figma link' and 'cancel the yoga', so the command 'cancel the yoga' is made part of the note.\",'''@c1 syntax.clause form=imperative verb=\"book\" modifier=\"tomorrow\" complement=$n1\n@n1 syntax.nominal dependent=\"a\" dependent=\"Design\" head=\"sync\"\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"with\" from=$n1 to=$n2\n@n2 syntax.nominal head=\"Ana\"\n@r2 syntax.relation attachment=ambiguous marker=\"at\" from=$c1 to=$n3\n@n3 syntax.nominal head=\"3\"\n@r3 syntax.relation attachment=ambiguous marker=\"with\" from=$c1 to=$n4\n@n4 syntax.nominal head=\"notes\"\n@c2 syntax.clause form=nonfinite verb=\"Share\" complement=$n5\n@n5 syntax.nominal dependent=\"Figma\" head=\"link\"\n@r4 syntax.relation from=$n4 to=$c2\n@c3 syntax.clause form=imperative verb=\"cancel\" complement=$n6\n@n6 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"yoga\"\n@k1 syntax.coordination conjunction=\"and\" conjunct=$c1 conjunct=$c3'''),\n(312,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'if there's still time on Wednesday at 2' is tied to 'add a meeting with Priya', and the reported 'it's about the parental leave handover' is tied to 'note' through 'that'.\",None),\n(313,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'Notes' is the subject of 'should say' and 'print 10 copies of the deck' is placed beside it, which the next layer can read as its content.\",None),\n(314,\"L1\",\"'meeting with Ana, note: bring the contract' has no verb, yet 'meeting' is written as the verb of a nonfinite clause, so a noun is made the verb and the fragment is lost.\",'''@n1 syntax.nominal head=\"meeting\"\n@n2 syntax.nominal head=\"Ana\"\n@n3 syntax.nominal head=\"note\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=fragment complement=$n1\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"with\" from=$n1 to=$n2\n@r2 syntax.relation from=$c1 to=$n3\n@c2 syntax.clause form=nonfinite verb=\"bring\" complement=$n4\n@n4 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"contract\"\n@r3 syntax.relation from=$n3 to=$c2'''),\n(315,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'call' may be read as the verb of the command, and 'with Lee', 'tomorrow' and the 'agenda' fragment are all placed in the sentence.\",None),\n(317,\"L1\",\"'what went wrong with the release' is the content of the notes and states something, yet it is written form=interrogative.\",'''@n1 syntax.nominal head=\"Retro\"\n@n2 syntax.nominal head=\"Friday\"\n@n3 syntax.nominal head=\"notes\"\n@n4 syntax.nominal head=\"what\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=declarative verb=\"went\" modifier=\"wrong\" subject=$n4\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"with\" from=$c1 to=$n5\n@n5 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"release\"\n@c2 syntax.clause form=fragment complement=$n1 complement=$n2 complement=$n3\n@k1 syntax.coordination conjunct=$c2 conjunct=$c1'''),\n(318,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'lunch with Lee Thursday' is a fragment with 'Thursday' tied to it, and 'remember the gift card' is a command joined beside it.\",None),\n(319,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'notes say parking is on level 2' keeps its clause, the content clause 'parking is on level 2' tied to it, and '2' tied to 'level'.\",None),\n(322,\"L8\",\"Accepted: the three names are the end of 'with', and 'at a time they're all available' ties the relative clause to 'a time'.\",None),\n(323,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'a 30 minute check-in' keeps its words, and 'at the earliest opening on Thursday' is tied from the clause with 'on Thursday' tied to the opening.\",None),\n(325,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'Lee and Ana are hard to pin down' is the subject of 'are' with the infinitive tied to it, and 'pick a time that works for both of them' and 'set up the meeting' are commands joined with it.\",None),\n(326,\"L8\",\"Accepted: 'the server went down last night' and 'Get me a meeting with Mihai at the soonest free moment' are each placed, with the place tied to the command.\",None),\n(327,\"L8\",\